{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787030378092430001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"covert-nickel-yearling","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"77136c5f36ac27f900ab13d744d2956da63f4a791fea9a5245b572e79fac266a","event_uuid":"d0556d26-6dfc-4fe5-beac-e83e0c9585b1","position":{"commit_sha":"790046c3f19b62e4518a5eb2d73ad533138b081d","position":"1787028165530346001-d0556d26-6dfc-4fe5-beac-e83e0c9585b1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"eeb8cd921c0996a10de86a52bfb7428ba02dbf520c0fdc779f00f93779ae592e","event_uuid":"eb7be043-72da-4882-8860-aca165a3c1a4","position":{"commit_sha":"817fec1c9b3a85897faf02d99c60b1c1d051957d","position":"1787028177154075001-eb7be043-72da-4882-8860-aca165a3c1a4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"081ab47307361571b3ed25c66324d153c29ade1b206cad0b72d9adbaf75b3559","event_uuid":"e2fa8369-5538-4dc2-aeee-904e027e4c8b","position":{"commit_sha":"210a2214faf5032f5ef35d14719cfb4dccf1dfba","position":"1787028195563623001-e2fa8369-5538-4dc2-aeee-904e027e4c8b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787028165530346001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nS1 provides one budgeted atomic summary executor and S2 provides immutable plans, but compound legacy dispatch can replay successful early work and conflates applied, deferred, and failed outcomes.\n\n## Outcome\nAdd a provider-neutral coordinator and failure policy for update, delete, probe, clean-label, repair-property, and conflict plans. Execute atomic desired postconditions in dependency order and re-observe only remaining drift after partial success.\n\n## Plan\n1. Define normalized success, recovered, deferred, permanent, `commit_unknown`, exhausted-transient, and skipped dispositions with ticket/endpoint/tenant/provider/global scope.\n2. Consume immutable plans, enforce their dependencies, and call adapter atomic operations through the S1 budget.\n3. Preserve proven earlier postconditions after a late failure; re-observe and plan only remaining drift instead of replaying the compound mutation.\n4. Treat already-gone delete as idempotent success, ticket-local 404/permanent 4xx as ticket-scoped, and authoritative broad failures only at their declared scope.\n5. Produce exact per-ticket applied/failed/deferred/skipped/recovered outcomes without implementing a fuse yet.\n\n## Testing\nCoordinator tables cover dependencies, partial update, delete, ticket-local 404, permanent 4xx, auth/quota/rate scopes, and independent continuation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Non-create plans execute atomic postconditions once in dependency order.\n- [ ] Late failure preserves proven earlier success and re-observes only remaining drift.\n- [ ] Already-gone delete is idempotent success.\n- [ ] Ticket-local and permanent failures isolate the ticket, while authoritative broad failures stop only their declared scope.\n- [ ] Independent tickets and endpoints continue.\n- [ ] Per-ticket outcome fields and tallies distinguish applied, failed, deferred, skipped, and recovered work exactly.\n\n## Out of scope\nFinite-pass fuse thresholds and production family cutover remain later S3 tasks.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/coordinator.py","reason":"Provider-neutral per-ticket non-create coordinator."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/failure_policy.py","reason":"Normalized disposition and failure-scope policy."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"Execute one atomic plan with partial-postcondition accounting."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_coordinator.py","reason":"Dependency, partial-success, scope, and exact-outcome tables."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_stale_binding_404.py","reason":"Ticket-local 404 isolation regression."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","28a3-a62d-6345-44a0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"28a3-a62d-6345-44a0","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp03","coordinator","tdd"],"ticket_id":"d0ec-da23-32ba-47c6","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S3 T1 — Coordinate atomic non-create postconditions","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_coordinator.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_stale_binding_404.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC6","dd_text":"Atomic order, partial success, delete idempotency, scope isolation, continuation, and exact outcomes"}]},"source_event_uuids":["d0556d26-6dfc-4fe5-beac-e83e0c9585b1","eb7be043-72da-4882-8860-aca165a3c1a4","e2fa836